# Title: PUA - Sysinternals Tools Execution - Registry
# ID: c7da8edc-49ae-45a2-9e61-9fd860e4e73d
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-08-24
# Tags: attack.resource-development, attack.t1588.002
# Description: Detects the execution of some potentially unwanted tools such as PsExec, Procdump, etc. (part of the Sysinternals suite) via the creation of the "accepteula" registry key.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog ((registry_key_name="*\\Active Directory Explorer*" OR registry_key_name="*\\Handle*" OR registry_key_name="*\\LiveKd*" OR registry_key_name="*\\Process Explorer*" OR registry_key_name="*\\ProcDump*" OR registry_key_name="*\\PsExec*" OR registry_key_name="*\\PsLoglist*" OR registry_key_name="*\\PsPasswd*" OR registry_key_name="*\\SDelete*" OR registry_key_name="*\\Sysinternals*") AND registry_key_name="*\\EulaAccepted")
